# Cloudflare Pages security headers, applied to every route.
#
# CSP ships REPORT-ONLY on purpose: Astro inlines the small island scripts
# (<script type="module"> in the built HTML), which `script-src 'self'` will FLAG in a
# browser's console without blocking anything. Before promoting to an enforcing
# Content-Security-Policy, externalize or hash those inline scripts and confirm zero
# violations in DevTools. Report-only cannot break the site; enforcing can, silently.
#
# No report-uri/report-to destination is set: violations surface in each visitor's console,
# which is enough for the pre-enforcement verification this phase is for. Add a collector
# (report-to + a Reporting-Endpoints header, or a service like Sentry) only if central
# aggregation is wanted later — it is not required to promote this to an enforcing CSP.
#
# HSTS (Strict-Transport-Security) is intentionally NOT set here — it stays a Cloudflare
# dashboard toggle (founder's call).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'
